# Ephemeris validation against JPL Horizons (DE441)

Processed Horizons tables fetched 2026-10-05/06 are in data/horizons (headers list centre, site and columns; the raw API responses and request metadata were not archived). All residuals below are computed by this script.

## Geocentric table: 74 epochs at 10-day spacing, 2027-01-01 .. 2028-12-31
- astrometric (light-time-corrected) range minus Horizons delta: rms 0.0004 km, max 0.0010 km
- sub-Earth, geometric (orientation and Moon at t): lon rms 0.00400 max 0.00577 deg; lat rms 0.00027 max 0.00053 deg
- sub-Earth, astrometric (retarded vector, orientation at t - tau): lon rms 0.00000 max 0.00001 deg; lat rms 0.00001 max 0.00001 deg
- sub-Earth, apparent (astrometric + stellar aberration): lon rms 0.00400 max 0.00575 deg; lat rms 0.00027 max 0.00053 deg
- sub-solar, geometric at t: lon rms 0.00551 max 0.00581 deg; lat rms 0.00011 max 0.00017 deg
- sub-solar, apparent like-for-like (see header): lon rms 0.00000 max 0.00001 deg; lat rms 0.00001 max 0.00001 deg
- sub-Earth, geometric, IAU (pck00011) orientation instead of DE421: lon rms 0.00427 max 0.00815 deg; lat rms 0.00112 max 0.00278 deg
Best-matching sub-Earth convention: sub-Earth, astrometric (retarded vector, orientation at t - tau). An angular residual of 0.006 deg corresponds to ~180 m of arc on the lunar surface, so the geometric screening (which uses geometric vectors) is accurate to ~0.01 deg, not to metres.
- PA->ME offset sign test (geometric sub-Earth): sign +1 lon rms 0.00400 deg; sign -1 lon rms 0.03769 deg (the +1 convention is used)

